   "why": "Python's json.loads, given bytes, detects UTF-16 and UTF-32 and reads them, so the door holds a record pushed as UTF-16. JSON exchanged between systems is UTF-8 (RFC 8259 section 8.1), and the port reads only UTF-8: the same bytes are refused request_malformed and nothing is stored."
